Let moles of $\mathrm{CO}_2=\mathrm{n}$ moles of $\mathrm{Ca}(\mathrm{OH})_2$ total initially $=2 \mathrm{n}$ excess $\mathrm{Ca}(\mathrm{OH})_2=\mathrm{n}$ gm equivalent of $\mathrm{Ca}(\mathrm{OH})_2=\mathrm{gm}$ equivalent of HCl
$\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{n} \times 2=0.1 \times \frac{40}{1000} \times 1 \\
& \mathrm{n}=2 \times 10^{-3}
\end{aligned}$

Volume of $\mathrm{CO}_2=2 \times 10^{-3} \times 22400=44.8 \mathrm{~cm}^3$

